Reason: patches 0077 and 0078 follow tile_delete by rewriting the whole tile run (every later array index moves down
one) and every cell of the tile-skip grid: on the console that was ~300 µs a delete, and crumbling sand in rm_a3h04
deletes 10 to 16 tiles a frame (1.5 to 3.3 ms of those frames). A delete now leaves its entry in the run, marked dead:
entries hold a pseudo index (the tile's array index when the run was built; adds take the next ones), and the deleted
pseudo indices are kept in order, so a tile's array index is its pseudo index less the deleted ones below it. The next
merge writes the live tiles with their array indices, as before, and the rank of every pseudo index; the grid's cells
hold pseudo indices and the query turns them into ranks, so a delete only moves the runs' bounds. After 1,024 deletes
the run and grid are built again. The draw list and the tiles drawn are the same.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

